# board speed's slack (rinc_boardSlack): a frame a little past the board's 60th of a second (115 lines of
# text, about 18 ms there) takes two frames as a developer sees it (rinc -board), and one playing
# (rinc -board -play, as an exported game and a page do), so twice as many draws in a second
draws := 0
told := false
draw* :: proc()
  draws += 1
  for i in 0..<115 do pc.print("forty characters of text, to be printed!", {0, i % 24 * 10}, 7)
  if pc.appTime() >= 0.9 and not told
    told = true
    log("board slack: draws by 0.9 s:", draws)
  end
end
